{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+\\frac{5\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{29\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{41\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{24},\\frac{17\\pi }{24},\\frac{29\\pi }{24},\\frac{41\\pi }{24}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{17\\pi }{24},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi }{24}=\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffc447bd29a74487b8b52b64f8599a39d89e7b16d550ddaff8444c367b721a85"} {"question" "q-8479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{17{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{85\\pi }{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffc447bd29a74487b8b52b64f8599a39d89e7b16d550ddaff8444c367b721a85"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{24}"] ["math" "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\pi }{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\pi }{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-8557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={135}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={315}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘},{135}^{∘},{225}^{∘},{315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 135=6\\,075.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffc447bd29a74487b8b52b64f8599a39d89e7b16d550ddaff8444c367b721a85"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\,005"] ["math" "3\\,265"] ["math" "3\\,526"] ["math" "6\\,075"] ["math" "6\\,750"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-82373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\,075"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $3tan\\,(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-3\\sqrt{3}=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-3\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n+1)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{19\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{7\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{13\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{19\\pi }{12}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffc447bd29a74487b8b52b64f8599a39d89e7b16d550ddaff8444c367b721a85"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\pi}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328350" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{19\\pi}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+{45}^{∘})=1,$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=-{180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-{90}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={-180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={-90}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ffc447bd29a74487b8b52b64f8599a39d89e7b16d550ddaff8444c367b721a85"} {"question" "q-328369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f239b4351738baf70ac773e2c1e11dda09c0e12bda"} {"question" "q-328369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-180"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062449/state.json" "file_sha256" "1db5a97a80cdb7cdf094e1f